# Level 0 — Initial SSH Connection

## Level Goal
Establish an SSH connection to the Bandit game server.

## Description
This is the entry point to the Bandit wargame. SSH (Secure Shell) is a cryptographic protocol for securely accessing remote machines — a foundational skill for any Linux or security professional.

## Approach
The first step was to resolve the server's IP address:

```bash
nslookup bandit.labs.overthewire.org
```

This confirmed the server was reachable. I then connected via SSH on the non-standard port 2220:

```bash
ssh bandit0@bandit.labs.overthewire.org -p 2220
```

Entered `bandit0` as the password when prompted. Connection established successfully.

## Key Takeaway
The `-p 2220` flag overrides SSH's default port 22. Every level in Bandit uses this port.
